# DTF tier manifest: scanner-adapter-cache-partition
#   (artifact-keeper#5943, PR #5949: a 1.12.0 adapter feature, not on the
#   1.11.x line)
# Profile-set: filesystem + trivy (the scanner-adapter sidecar,
# SCANNER_ADAPTER_IMAGE). The oracle starts two more containers on the slot
# network with `docker run` and removes them by name on exit:
#   ak-dtf<slot>-sacp-trivysrv  a trivy server (pinned by digest, alias
#                               dtf-trivysrv) that the adapter uses in client
#                               mode: one shared analysis cache
#   ak-dtf<slot>-sacp-reg       fixtures/ocireg.py, a read-only OCI registry
#                               answering as dtf-rega:5000 and dtf-regb:5000,
#                               the registry hosts of two Artifact Keeper
#                               instances that share the adapter
# and recreates the adapter with fixtures/trivy-server.yml (client mode,
# partition prefix "dtf"), plus fixtures/registry-mode.yml for the FIX cases.
# Images are built at run time by fixtures/mkimage.py: alpine-shaped layers
# listing libcrypto1.1 1.1.1c-r0 (Trivy reports its CVEs), each with a unique
# mark so every case starts on fresh cache keys, and "forged" images whose
# single layer holds no packages but whose config claims a genuine layer's
# diff ID.
# NETWORK: the trivy server downloads the Trivy DB from ghcr.io once per run
# (~130 MiB).
#
# WHAT IS GATED
#   #5943 trivy keys a layer's cached analysis by the diff ID the image config
#         claims. With one partition per adapter (SCANNER_TRIVY_CACHE_PARTITION,
#         static), anyone who can push to one instance's registry can plant an
#         analysis that another instance's scan of a genuine image reuses: a
#         false clean. SCANNER_TRIVY_CACHE_PARTITION_MODE=registry derives the
#         partition per request from the registry host.
#
# THE CASES
#   (CONTROL) default mode: a genuine image on a fresh cache key reports its
#     vulnerabilities; /api/v1/metadata has no partition-mode property.
#   (CONTROL) default mode is unchanged: forged image via host A, then the
#     genuine image via host B reports 0 (one shared partition, as before),
#     and a request without a registry host is still accepted (202).
#   (FIX #5943) registry mode is applied: metadata reports
#     properties."env.SCANNER_TRIVY_CACHE_PARTITION_MODE"=registry, and
#     neither metadata nor the startup log shows the partition value.
#   (FIX #5943) registry mode: forged image via host A, then the genuine image
#     via host B reports the same count as on a fresh key. Pre-fix: 0.
#   (FIX #5943) registry mode refuses a request with no registry host (empty
#     or scheme-only registry.url) with 400. Pre-fix: 202.
#
# RED  backend :main + adapter sha-ff3335f (main): 3 of 6, the three FIX
#      cases fail. GREEN backend :main + the adapter built from #5949: 6 of 6.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: back-to-back report polls.
COVERS="5943"
PROFILES="storage.filesystem scanners.trivy"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
